From 0062e03e2d757a12298df21cf6b91f3abf18cb8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab <homelab@emrys.dev>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] auth: land a first header login on a Spotify cookie
 page

Header-only identity is enough to log in, not to track. is_user_logged_in()
is false while users.cookies_json is NULL, and the per-user listener that
records plays is built from those cookies - so a first login with no stored
session would reach a dashboard that can never record anything.

A header-authenticated account with no stored Spotify session is now sent to
/connect-spotify, which carries the same cookie instructions as the login
page and saves the pasted session. This is also where an expired session is
replaced. The ownership rule is unchanged and now lives in one place
(verifyCookiesForEmail): the Spotify account's email must match the trusted
email, because the Listener marks a mismatched session as contamination and
refuses to record it.

get_current_user_or_redirect() also stops treating listener health as
authentication for a header-established session. Otherwise a Spotify outage
or a lapsed cookie would redirect to /login, which this mode serves as 404.

Standalone login keeps its exact behaviour: routes/auth.py's _verifiedCookies
delegates to the same helper it used to inline.
